ifa/issues/133, the separator question -- under the start-merged default two arity-1 list literals share a CreationSet and nothing separates them. Arity is currently the ONLY working separator for list literals, and it correctly says nothing here since both are arity 1. Their slot types differ (str vs nil) but that union IS representable, so no demand is raised at the merge; it only becomes irrepresentable several contours downstream, by which time the literals are long merged. Flips to PASS when the separator set gains another REPRESENTATION property knowable at construction -- the slot's basic-type kind being the obvious candidate (ifa/129 step 3).
